* Exported names

In Go, a name is exported if it begins with a capital letter.
For example, ⟪GTI18N_38b9c70e_000001⟫Pizza⟪GTI18N_38b9c70e_000002⟫ is an exported name, as is ⟪GTI18N_38b9c70e_000003⟫Pi⟪GTI18N_38b9c70e_000004⟫, which is exported from
the ⟪GTI18N_38b9c70e_000005⟫math⟪GTI18N_38b9c70e_000006⟫ package.

⟪GTI18N_38b9c70e_000007⟫pizza⟪GTI18N_38b9c70e_000008⟫ and ⟪GTI18N_38b9c70e_000009⟫pi⟪GTI18N_38b9c70e_000010⟫ do not start with a capital letter, so they are not exported.

When importing a package, you can refer only to its exported names.
Any "unexported" names are not accessible from outside the package.

Run the code. Notice the error message.

To fix the error, rename ⟪GTI18N_38b9c70e_000011⟫math.pi⟪GTI18N_38b9c70e_000012⟫ to ⟪GTI18N_38b9c70e_000013⟫math.Pi⟪GTI18N_38b9c70e_000014⟫ and try it again.

